findings.body:
**A comment-only push leaves the PR stuck on `pr/ci-pending`**

This delta rewrote the line, and it still treats any individual `pending` status as a running check:

```js
if (runs.some((c) => c.status !== "completed") || combined.statuses.some((s) => s.state === "pending")) {
  return "pr/ci-pending";
}
```

The review preflight sets a `pending` status on purpose, and it is a final marker, not an in-progress one. On a push that only changes comments or prose (`preflight.utils.ts:244`, `skip-comment-only`), it sets the status and then skips the review (`tools/review/src/review-preflight.script.ts` L198-206):

```ts
// Pending, not green, on the PR at this head, so a merge here is not read as
// reviewed; nothing requires the check, so it never blocks the merge.
markNotReviewed(headSha, `Not reviewed: only comments and prose changed since ${priorSha?.slice(0, 7)}`);
out("skip", "true");
```

With `skip=true`, the poster and every later step that could write `claude-review` are skipped (`claude-code-review.yml` L398, L439, L453, L469). That status stays `pending` on that SHA for good. The `workflow_run` recompute then labels the PR `pr/ci-pending` ("Checks are still running"), even though nothing is running. Waiting never clears it. Only a code push or an `@claude review` does.

The pre-delta `combined.state === "pending"` behaved the same way. The workflow is new in this PR, so it ships with this behavior. The preflight's intent, "not read as reviewed", rules out `pr/ready`, but it does not make "checks are still running" true.

Possible fixes (your design call):
- Don't count the preflight's "Not reviewed" marker as pending, e.g. `!(s.context === "claude-review" && s.description?.startsWith("Not reviewed"))`.
- Map it to a distinct, honest label.
- Have the preflight signal "not reviewed" without using `pending`.

